#
# The ground hash covers every triple with no blank node on either
# end, which is canonical as it stands. The blank-node hash covers the
# rest, with each blank node named by a hash of its own content
# instead of the parser's label -- label-free without URDNA2015,
# which is impractical at this size.
#
# Anchors are named subjects; blank nodes print as _:_ because parser
# -assigned labels differ run to run and would churn the file.
#

